1
00:00:01,020 --> 00:00:03,400
我最棒的一次偶遇明星经验
What was my best brush with celebrity?

2
00:00:03,680 --> 00:00:05,440
这真是个好问题
Oh, this is such a good one.

3
00:00:06,360 --> 00:00:08,400
有次我在洗车店看到了杰克·尼科尔森
One time I saw Jack Nicholson at the car wash.

4
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:09,840
我简直不想再说了
I can't go through this again.

5
00:00:09,960 --> 00:00:12,049
杰克·尼科尔森不会开一辆贴着
Jack Nicholson does not drive a Hyundai Odyssey

6
00:00:12,049 --> 00:00:14,339
"宗教共存"的现代奥德赛 小卡
with a Co-Exist bumper sticker, Cam.

7
00:00:14,580 --> 00:00:15,878
在橱柜行业干了那么多年
Being in the closet business,

8
00:00:15,878 --> 00:00:17,280
我遇到过许多明星
I met a lot of famous people.

9
00:00:17,280 --> 00:00:18,300
我不能提名字
I can't name names,

10
00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:21,100
就这么说吧 那人是老大
but let's just say it's someone who's the boss.

11
00:00:21,280 --> 00:00:22,760
你遇到布鲁斯·斯普林斯汀吗
You met Bruce Springsteen?

12
00:00:22,820 --> 00:00:25,040
-不 是托尼·丹扎 -电视剧里的吗
- No, Tony Danza. - Oh, from the TV show?

13
00:00:25,240 --> 00:00:26,480
那部剧女主才是老大
Nah, she was the boss.

14
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:27,840
个人见解不同啦
It's open to interpretation.

15
00:00:28,540 --> 00:00:30,980
我在商场看见了圣诞老人
I saw Santa Claus at the mall.

16
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:35,780
《不知情的卡斯尔小姐》
"The Unwitting Miss Castle."

17
00:00:35,780 --> 00:00:36,580
讲的是什么
What's that about?

18
00:00:36,880 --> 00:00:38,460
讲的是不同时代中
It's about three persecuted women

19
00:00:38,460 --> 00:00:39,480
三个被迫害的女人
in different time periods,

20
00:00:39,480 --> 00:00:42,360
或者是一个特别倒霉的时间旅行者
or one time traveler with incredibly bad luck.

21
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:43,200
我不知道是哪个
I don't know which.

22
00:00:43,660 --> 00:00:45,060
我莫名其妙加入了
Somehow, I was able to join

23
00:00:45,060 --> 00:00:46,680
一个非常排外的读书俱乐部
a very exclusive book club

24
00:00:46,680 --> 00:00:48,720
里面都是超高智商的女人
filled with the most intelligent women.

25
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:50,780
我总是无法令她们感到惊艳
I can never seem to impress them.

26
00:00:50,880 --> 00:00:52,580
她们会用"枯苗望雨"这种高级词
They use words like "Sanguine."

27
00:00:52,900 --> 00:00:55,160
我不想看起来像是个傻瓜 所以我也用
I don't want to look like an idiot, so I use it, too.

28
00:00:55,160 --> 00:00:58,320
这是不是你听到过的最"枯苗望雨"的东西
Isn't that the most sanguine thing you ever heard?

29
00:00:59,120 --> 00:01:00,080
你用错了
You're not using it right.

30
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:03,460
同一章我都读了八次了
I've read the same chapter eight times --

31
00:01:03,900 --> 00:01:04,640
还是不懂
still don't get it.

32
00:01:04,880 --> 00:01:07,520
就说"这反映了社会现状"
Just say, "It holds a mirror up to society."

33
00:01:07,720 --> 00:01:09,500
你会得个C 顺利脱身
You'll get your "C" and get out of there.

34
00:01:11,080 --> 00:01:13,020
-早上好 -嗨
- Good morning. - Hi.

35
00:01:13,720 --> 00:01:14,960
这年轻人是谁
Who's that young thing?

36
00:01:15,360 --> 00:01:17,879
怎么打扮成这样 像电视剧的人一样犀利啊
Wow, what's up with the outfit, Mod Squad?

37
00:01:17,879 --> 00:01:19,220
是啊 我要...
Oh, yeah, I'm, uh...

38
00:01:19,220 --> 00:01:20,918
我要带人看房
I'm showing a house to someone.

39
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:22,440
我不想说是谁
I'd rather not say who it is.

40
00:01:22,540 --> 00:01:23,480
我完全理解
I totally get that.

41
00:01:23,480 --> 00:01:25,240
是酷玩乐队的主唱克里斯·马汀
It's Chris Martin from Coldplay.

42
00:01:25,840 --> 00:01:28,000
-拜托 真的吗 -不是什么大事啦
- Come on, really? - It's not a big deal.

43
00:01:28,180 --> 00:01:29,520
说这话的人昨晚花了大半晚上时间
Says the man who spent most of last night

44
00:01:29,520 --> 00:01:30,860
往牛仔裤上缝花
sewing that flower onto his jeans.

45
00:01:31,020 --> 00:01:32,060
好吧 这真的是件大事
Okay, it's a really big deal.

46
00:01:32,140 --> 00:01:33,620
我要跟一个唱出我感受的歌手见面了
I'm meeting the man who sings how I feel.

47
00:01:33,800 --> 00:01:36,180
是啊 他的音乐非常"枯苗望雨"
Yes, his music is so sanguine.

48
00:01:36,330 --> 00:01:37,934
比上次强
Eh, closer.

49
00:01:38,500 --> 00:01:39,900
我从来都不是很喜欢酷玩乐队
Never been a big Coldplay guy.

50
00:01:40,020 --> 00:01:41,700
我更喜欢嘻哈 死亡金属
I'm more into hip-hop, death metal,

51
00:01:41,860 --> 00:01:42,480
《小美人鱼》
"Little Mermaid."

52
00:01:43,280 --> 00:01:45,320
那电影对我小时候影响好大啊
That one really imprinted on me back in the day.

53
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:47,300
我肚子很难受
My stomach feels weird.

54
00:01:47,540 --> 00:01:48,740
你也许只是紧张
You're probably just nervous.

55
00:01:48,920 --> 00:01:50,520
也许你需要有人陪你去
Ooh, maybe you need someone to come with you.

56
00:01:50,540 --> 00:01:52,857
不要 他是去买房的 不是谈论音乐的
No, he's there to buy a house, not talk about music,

57
00:01:52,857 --> 00:01:54,000
所以我压根都不会提
which is why I'm not even gonna mention

58
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:55,119
我也是歌曲作家
that I'm a songwriter, too.

59
00:01:55,119 --> 00:01:56,535
你就写了一首歌
Oh, you wrote one song.

60
00:01:56,700 --> 00:01:57,978
歌里有我想说的一切了
I said everything I had to say.

61
00:01:57,978 --> 00:01:59,060
房地产经纪人的故事
About a realtor.

62
00:01:59,060 --> 00:02:00,280
是关于人生
It was about life!

63
00:02:00,300 --> 00:02:01,960
难怪读书俱乐部的人嘲笑你
This is why they mock you at book club.

64
00:02:15,300 --> 00:02:16,880
我可以聊聊某一次
Oh, here's a brush with celebrity

65
00:02:16,880 --> 00:02:17,960
和明星的偶遇
I can actually talk about.

66
00:02:18,320 --> 00:02:20,040
去年夏天 我被要求
Last summer, I was called upon

67
00:02:20,040 --> 00:02:22,620
参与最美式的传统
to participate in the most American of traditions --

68
00:02:23,060 --> 00:02:24,380
摆脱陪审团的职责
getting out of jury duty.

69
00:02:24,880 --> 00:02:27,240
您有任何跟执法机构接触的经验吗
Do you have any experience with law enforcement?

70
00:02:27,620 --> 00:02:28,176
多了去了
Big time.

71
00:02:28,176 --> 00:02:30,360
我不信任警察
I-I don't trust, uh, cops.

72
00:02:30,360 --> 00:02:32,240
而且我鄙视被抢劫的人
Also, I despise robbery victims.

73
00:02:32,440 --> 00:02:33,480
他们才是真正的罪犯
They're the real criminals

74
00:02:33,480 --> 00:02:35,019
占用了我们的审判系统
for clogging up our court system.

75
00:02:35,019 --> 00:02:36,260
想得美 3号陪审员
Nice try, Juror 3.

76
00:02:36,260 --> 00:02:38,200
那么经济困难呢
What about economic hardship?

77
00:02:38,240 --> 00:02:39,660
上次我没去工作时
The last time I missed work,

78
00:02:39,760 --> 00:02:41,902
加州橱柜市场都崩溃了
the California closet market collapsed.

79
00:02:41,902 --> 00:02:43,830
有人认为那导致了洛杉矶暴动
Some people think that caused the L.A. Riot.

80
00:02:45,140 --> 00:02:46,660
看来我该收声了
I must be done talking.

81
00:02:46,860 --> 00:02:48,038
我要生了
I'm going into labor.

82
00:02:48,038 --> 00:02:50,358
女士 一切都会没事的
Ma'am, Ma'am, everything's gonna be all right.

83
00:02:50,358 --> 00:02:53,020
法警 帮助一下11号陪审员
Bailiff, help Juror 11 with anything she needs,

84
00:02:53,020 --> 00:02:54,200
叫下一位替换陪审员
and bring in the next alternate.

85
00:02:54,460 --> 00:02:56,000
作为她无痛分娩法的教练
Uh, as her Lamaze coach,

86
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:57,660
我想我该去走廊...
I think I should probably be out in the hall wi--

87
00:03:02,780 --> 00:03:03,700
特里·布拉德肖
Terry Bradshaw.

88
00:03:04,060 --> 00:03:05,460
我爱特里·布拉德肖
I love Terry Bradshaw!

89
00:03:06,240 --> 00:03:08,760
11号陪审员 有什么原因会阻止你
Juror 11, is there anything that might prevent you

90
00:03:08,760 --> 00:03:10,480
有效地履行陪审团义务吗
from serving effectively on this jury?

91
00:03:10,700 --> 00:03:12,540
日程没有冲突 法官大人
No scheduling conflicts, Your Honor.

92
00:03:13,180 --> 00:03:14,900
然而我现在
However, I am going through

93
00:03:14,900 --> 00:03:16,280
正经历一段困难的时期
kind of a rough patch right now.

94
00:03:16,280 --> 00:03:18,060
我失去了我死党
You see, I lost my best friend.

95
00:03:18,240 --> 00:03:19,600
还是他刚找到了一位新死党
Or did he just find one?

96
00:03:19,720 --> 00:03:21,260
但我很高兴履行义务
But I'm happy to serve.

97
00:03:21,520 --> 00:03:23,540
我相信美国司法制度
I believe in the American legal system,

98
00:03:23,540 --> 00:03:25,380
靠的就是团队合作
and I believe it's all about teamwork.

99
00:03:26,880 --> 00:03:29,060
真是个"触地得分"的好答案啊 冠军
That's a touchdown of an answer, champ.

100
00:03:29,520 --> 00:03:30,960
这位女士
Uh, this lady here...

101
00:03:31,600 --> 00:03:32,660
我决定也当陪审员
put me down for that.

102
00:03:32,820 --> 00:03:34,380
你准备好接受正义制裁了吗
Are you ready for some justice?

103
00:03:37,700 --> 00:03:38,640
天啊
Oh, my God.

104
00:03:38,900 --> 00:03:40,120
怎么了 有明星吗
What? A celebrity?

105
00:03:40,520 --> 00:03:42,980
-是山姆·安威尔马克 -谁
- It's Sam Anvilmaker. - Who?

106
00:03:42,980 --> 00:03:44,800
他写了《遗忘者和被遗忘者》
He wrote "The Forgetters and the Forgotten"?

107
00:03:45,300 --> 00:03:46,360
《美国式闹剧》
"Farce, American Style"?

108
00:03:46,700 --> 00:03:47,920
《读这本书就滚蛋》
"Screw You For Reading This"?

109
00:03:48,020 --> 00:03:49,060
"这到底什么情况"
What the hell is happening?

110
00:03:49,180 --> 00:03:50,280
对 这也是他写的
Yes, that one, too!

111
00:03:50,500 --> 00:03:51,886
他是我最喜欢的编剧
He's my favorite playwright.

112
00:03:51,886 --> 00:03:52,940
你为什么不过去
Why don't you go over

113
00:03:52,940 --> 00:03:54,140
告诉他你是他粉丝
and tell him that you're a fan?

114
00:03:54,260 --> 00:03:55,660
也许他会给你一些建议
Maybe he can give you some advice.

115
00:03:55,820 --> 00:03:58,080
不不 我不想打扰他
No, no, I wouldn't want to bother him.

116
00:03:58,260 --> 00:03:59,720
他不喜欢被打扰是出了名的
He's notoriously private.

117
00:03:59,840 --> 00:04:01,320
他在蒙大纳某处的一棵
He writes in a hollowed-out tree

118
00:04:01,320 --> 00:04:02,200
挖空的树干里头写作
somewhere in Montana.

119
00:04:02,460 --> 00:04:03,460
别紧张
Don't be nervous.

120
00:04:03,680 --> 00:04:04,760
我就是感觉这样不太好
It just doesn't feel right.

121
00:04:05,060 --> 00:04:07,500
曼尼 如果有人像你这么喜欢我的作品
Manny, if somebody admired my work as much as this,

122
00:04:07,520 --> 00:04:08,760
我会很想知道的
I would like to know.

123
00:04:10,040 --> 00:04:11,320
-去吧 -好吧
- Go. - Okay.

124
00:04:12,100 --> 00:04:13,260
那我过去了
Here we go.

125
00:04:17,340 --> 00:04:20,140
-打扰一下 安威尔马克先生 -让我猜猜
- Uh, excuse me, Mr. Anvilmaker? - Let me guess --

126
00:04:20,440 --> 00:04:22,820
我是你想成为编剧的原因
I'm the reason you want to be a writer.

127
00:04:23,080 --> 00:04:23,920
是的 没错
Yeah, actually.

128
00:04:23,940 --> 00:04:26,121
您的第一部剧改变了我对...
Your first play changed the way that I looked at --

129
00:04:26,121 --> 00:04:27,253
听我说 孩子
Look, listen, kid.

130
00:04:27,280 --> 00:04:28,700
我不是来这里收集
I'm not here to collect panties

131
00:04:28,700 --> 00:04:29,880
写着电话号码的内裤的
with phone numbers on them.

132
00:04:29,880 --> 00:04:32,660
我是来这里体验活着的那种
I'm here to experience the cold absurdity

133
00:04:32,660 --> 00:04:34,340
冷漠荒诞感
that is being alive.

134
00:04:34,820 --> 00:04:37,500
找别人崇拜去吧
So go and find someone else to venerate.

135
00:04:38,580 --> 00:04:41,000
很抱歉打扰你了
Oh, uh... Sorry for bothering you.

136
00:04:41,700 --> 00:04:42,600
给你一条写作小窍门
Here's a writing tip --

137
00:04:42,940 --> 00:04:44,840
让我看到你真为打扰我而感到抱歉
show me you're sorry for bothering me.

138
00:04:44,980 --> 00:04:46,140
而不是光动嘴皮子
Don't tell me.

139
00:04:46,440 --> 00:04:47,980
好了 来为这两个
Okay, let's take a picture

140
00:04:47,980 --> 00:04:49,800
新交的死党拍张合影
of the two new best friends.

141
00:04:49,800 --> 00:04:50,180
快靠近点儿
Come together.

142
00:04:50,300 --> 00:04:52,060
我就不该离开我的树
I should never have left my tree.

143
00:04:52,840 --> 00:04:54,740
我还在我们的干洗店看到了
And then, I saw Daniel Day-Lewis

144
00:04:54,740 --> 00:04:55,700
影帝丹尼尔·戴·路易斯
at our dry cleaner.

145
00:04:56,040 --> 00:04:57,700
不是他 真不是
Not him. No.

146
00:04:57,814 --> 00:04:59,820
我们真的看到名人是在
Uh, the time we actually saw a celebrity

147
00:04:59,820 --> 00:05:01,180
去年十二月
was last December

148
00:05:01,180 --> 00:05:03,060
我们去买园艺用品的时候
when we were shopping for gardening supplies.

149
00:05:03,220 --> 00:05:05,720
我永远不会忘记影帝演的林肯总统
I'll never forget the feeling of having Lincoln

150
00:05:05,720 --> 00:05:09,080
直勾勾地看着我的眼睛 然后说
look directly into my eyes and saying,

151
00:05:09,620 --> 00:05:12,580
"烧烤酱洗不掉"时候的感觉
"We couldn't get the barbecue sauce out."

152
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:15,340
我们不需要一人有一副
We both don't need a pair.

153
00:05:15,360 --> 00:05:16,520
我们可以共用啊
We can just share these.

154
00:05:16,520 --> 00:05:17,878
如果我想要我自己的呢
And what if I want my own?

155
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:19,200
我们什么东西都共用啊
We share everything.

156
00:05:19,300 --> 00:05:20,176
我们共用一把牙刷
We share a toothbrush.

157
00:05:20,176 --> 00:05:22,810
-有吗 -我的...我的天哪
- We do? Oh... - Oh, my -- Oh, my gosh.

158
00:05:22,810 --> 00:05:23,449
那个主持我们非常喜欢的
Hm? There's the guy who hosts

159
00:05:23,460 --> 00:05:24,787
家居大改造节目的家伙在那里
that home makeover show we love so much.

160
00:05:24,787 --> 00:05:25,600
-什么 在哪儿 -斯科特·亨特
- What? Where? - It's Scott Hunter.

161
00:05:25,600 --> 00:05:26,880
斯科特·亨特在那里
Scott Hunter is right over there.

162
00:05:27,400 --> 00:05:28,660
每一周 斯科特·亨特
Every week, Scott Hunter,

163
00:05:28,700 --> 00:05:30,460
《花您一点时间》的主持人
the host of "I Beg Your Garden,"

164
00:05:30,660 --> 00:05:33,078
会在家居店挑选不知情的两口子
selects an unsuspecting couple at a home store.

165
00:05:33,078 --> 00:05:35,787
对 他会拍他们的肩膀 然后说
Yeah, he taps them on the shoulder and says,

166
00:05:36,180 --> 00:05:37,020
"花您一点时间"
"I beg your garden."

167
00:05:37,100 --> 00:05:38,520
什么 我的天啊 真的假的
What?! Oh, my God! I can't believe it!

168
00:05:38,680 --> 00:05:40,240
每次都这样
That's how it goes every time.

169
00:05:40,480 --> 00:05:41,280
每次都是
Every time.

170
00:05:41,720 --> 00:05:42,919
-摄像机在哪里 -我知道
- Where are the cameras? - I know.

171
00:05:42,919 --> 00:05:44,560
要是我今天穿得更艳丽一点就好了
I wish I would've worn something more colorful.

172
00:05:44,560 --> 00:05:45,300
你知道吗
Okay, you know what?

173
00:05:45,440 --> 00:05:46,460
我们一定要上节目
We have to get on the show.

174
00:05:46,920 --> 00:05:48,700
你能想象我们后院被大改造吗
Can you imagine a backyard makeover,

175
00:05:48,700 --> 00:05:50,160
他会怎么改造我们的后院呢
what he would do with ours?

176
00:05:50,200 --> 00:05:51,760
没错 是三个字的
Yeah, one word, three syllables,

177
00:05:51,760 --> 00:05:54,117
开头是"小" 结尾是"凉亭"
starts with "Gah," ends with "zebo."

178
00:05:55,620 --> 00:05:56,020
小凉亭
Gazebo.

179
00:05:56,240 --> 00:05:57,960
-我爱死小凉亭了 -我也是
- I love gazebos. - I do, too!

180
00:05:57,960 --> 00:05:59,000
一开始想这个
Now that I'm thinking about it,

181
00:05:59,000 --> 00:05:59,877
我就非得要一个了
I have to have one.

182
00:05:59,877 --> 00:06:01,320
-天哪 -我们工作这么辛苦
- Oh, my gosh. - Wait, we work hard.

183
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:02,420
当然有权在后院
We deserve to stand in the shade

184
00:06:02,420 --> 00:06:03,700
-离草皮几英寸的地方乘凉 -就是
- a few inches off the ground. - Yeah.

185
00:06:03,860 --> 00:06:04,559
这样吧
Okay, you know what?

186
00:06:04,559 --> 00:06:06,596
-我们这就过去让他拍我们肩膀 -好
- Let's go get tapped. - Okay.

187
00:06:08,096 --> 00:06:09,120
那是什么东西
Hm, what's over here?

188
00:06:09,120 --> 00:06:11,260
不知道 天啊 米奇尔 你喜欢这个花盆吗
I don't know. Oh, my gosh, Mitchell, do you like this planter?

189
00:06:11,920 --> 00:06:13,000
把这放在我们那个
It would go great

190
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:16,217
荒芜老气得掉渣的后院里一定不错
in our hopelessly outdated and neglected backyard.

191
00:06:16,217 --> 00:06:17,740
你喜欢我就喜欢
Well, I love it if you love it.

192
00:06:17,740 --> 00:06:19,218
那你觉得这些铺路材料怎么样
And what do you think of these pavers?

193
00:06:19,218 --> 00:06:21,000
我觉得那会跟我们
Oh, I think they go great with that gazebo

194
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:21,700
梦寐以求的小凉亭很搭的
we've always dreamed of having.

195
00:06:21,700 --> 00:06:22,680
拉倒吧 他走了
Oh, forget it. He's gone.

196
00:06:23,027 --> 00:06:25,114
我们做错什么了 我们很讨喜啊
W-What did we do wrong? We were pleasant.

197
00:06:25,360 --> 00:06:27,820
你猜怎么着 可能是我们太讨喜了
You know what? Maybe we were too nice.

198
00:06:27,820 --> 00:06:30,311
上这些节目的小两口总是各种闹矛盾
Couples on those shows always have conflict.

199
00:06:30,311 --> 00:06:31,240
-我们也是啊 -对啊
- So do we. - Yeah.

200
00:06:31,240 --> 00:06:32,856
我们有多久没有达成一致过了
When's the last time we agreed on anything.

201
00:06:32,856 --> 00:06:34,580
我们永远在斗嘴啊
We -- We're constantly bickering.

202
00:06:34,580 --> 00:06:36,500
是啊 虽然斗嘴有时会反应出更深层的东西
I know, sometimes it reveals something deeper,

203
00:06:36,500 --> 00:06:37,980
但并不总是如此
but not always.

204
00:06:38,120 --> 00:06:38,880
来
You know what?

205
00:06:39,100 --> 00:06:41,520
我们去向他展示一下我们
Let's go show him our delightful brand

206
00:06:41,520 --> 00:06:42,400
毒舌得可爱的一面吧
of bitchy friction.

207
00:06:42,540 --> 00:06:44,380
跟我想的完全一样
I was thinking the exact same thing.

208
00:06:44,600 --> 00:06:46,360
-别总是跟我心有灵犀啊 -抱歉抱歉
- Stop seeing eye-to-eye with me. - Sorry, sorry.

209
00:06:46,360 --> 00:06:48,180
我们去找他 然后好好大吵一架
Let's go find him and drum up an argument.

210
00:06:48,300 --> 00:06:49,460
这主意太赞了
Yeah, terrific idea.

211
00:06:49,500 --> 00:06:50,840
我不是故意跟你有默契的
I'm not doing it on purpose.

212
00:06:51,040 --> 00:06:51,840
我只是...
I'm just...

213
00:06:57,800 --> 00:06:59,220
我这是怎么了
What is going on?

214
00:06:59,560 --> 00:07:00,120
我的...
My gro --

215
00:07:01,400 --> 00:07:02,400
简直是噩梦
This was a nightmare.

216
00:07:02,860 --> 00:07:04,120
我马上就要见到我的英雄
I was about to meet my hero,

217
00:07:04,220 --> 00:07:06,401
可我那个地方却莫名疼得要死
and I was experiencing this bizarre pain in --

218
00:07:06,401 --> 00:07:08,804
就是 下面那个地方
in my...nether region.

219
00:07:09,240 --> 00:07:10,320
等等 我是个成年男性
Wait, I'm a grown man.

220
00:07:10,320 --> 00:07:12,300
我应该不羞于直呼其名 我左边的蛋袋
I should be able to say it -- my left bean bag --

221
00:07:12,300 --> 00:07:12,880
我又没说出口
did it again.

222
00:07:13,360 --> 00:07:14,419
我的金玉蛋...
My tersticle --

223
00:07:14,419 --> 00:07:16,145
我想我没办法说得更直接了
That's as close as I think I'm gonna get.

224
00:07:16,820 --> 00:07:17,220
有人吗
Hello?

225
00:07:19,800 --> 00:07:20,940
欢迎欢迎欢迎
Welcome, welcome, welcome.

226
00:07:21,960 --> 00:07:23,361
-菲尔 -我是克里斯
- Phil. - Hey, I'm Chris.

227
00:07:23,361 --> 00:07:25,441
-你怎么了 -没怎么
- Hey, what's wrong? - Oh, nothing.

228
00:07:26,560 --> 00:07:27,940
你以为我本人会更帅些
You thought I'd be better looking.

229
00:07:28,480 --> 00:07:30,120
人们总这么以为 因为乐队其他人
People think that because the rest of the band

230
00:07:30,120 --> 00:07:31,643
-都长得跟霍比特人似的 -不不不
- look like hobbits. - No, no, no.

231
00:07:31,643 --> 00:07:32,776
只是 我只是有点...
It's -- It's a little --

232
00:07:32,800 --> 00:07:34,040
我喜欢你的花牛仔裤
I love your flower jeans.

233
00:07:34,220 --> 00:07:35,060
你在哪买的
Where did you get those?

234
00:07:35,240 --> 00:07:36,576
从商店买的
They're from a store.

235
00:07:36,576 --> 00:07:38,960
特别有我的风格 特别有我的风格
Well, they're very me. They're very me.

236
00:07:38,960 --> 00:07:39,960
你还记得店名吗
Do you remember the name of the store?

237
00:07:40,280 --> 00:07:42,000
其实是我自己绣的
Actually, I embroidered them myself.

238
00:07:42,400 --> 00:07:42,800
真了不起
Impressive.

239
00:07:43,720 --> 00:07:45,160
等你准备好后
When you're ready for it,

240
00:07:45,160 --> 00:07:47,700
你找件T恤 穿在长袖上衣外面
you get a T-shirt, you put it on top of a long-sleeve,

241
00:07:48,230 --> 00:07:51,260
这样大家就知道你有不止一件上衣了
then it lets everybody know you own multiple shirts.

242
00:07:51,260 --> 00:07:51,720
真厉害
Impressive.

243
00:07:52,299 --> 00:07:55,859
伙计 我们要不要这就开搞
So, mate, shall we have a trod-about?

244
00:07:56,200 --> 00:07:56,680
我受宠若惊
I'm flattered.

245
00:07:57,300 --> 00:07:58,600
但我觉得我们还是专业点
I'd rather just keep it professional,

246
00:07:58,980 --> 00:07:59,700
开始看房子吧
have a walk around.

247
00:07:59,700 --> 00:08:01,316
我不是那个意思
Oh, that's not what...I...meant...

248
00:08:08,320 --> 00:08:10,440
特里形单影只坐在那里
Terry was just sitting there by himself

249
00:08:10,440 --> 00:08:13,080
因为人们总是不敢去和最漂亮的姑娘搭讪
because everybody's always afraid to talk to the prettiest girl,

250
00:08:13,480 --> 00:08:14,140
除了这位
except this guy.

251
00:08:14,840 --> 00:08:16,200
自信是关键
It's all about confidence.

252
00:08:17,238 --> 00:08:18,374
打扰一下 布...
Excuse me, Mr. --

253
00:08:19,380 --> 00:08:20,386
打扰一下 布拉德肖先生
Excuse me, Mr. Bradshaw.

254
00:08:20,386 --> 00:08:22,560
杰·普里契特 三号陪审员
Jay Pritchett, juror number 3.

255
00:08:22,560 --> 00:08:23,516
特里 叫我特里就行
Terry. Call me Terry.

256
00:08:23,516 --> 00:08:25,120
-你好吗 特里 -挺好的 你呢
- How you doing, Terry? - Hi. Good. You?

257
00:08:25,120 --> 00:08:26,840
关于这起抢劫案
Hey, this robbery case, huh?

258
00:08:26,840 --> 00:08:28,320
我知道我们对案情还没有全面了解
Now, I know we don't have all the facts yet,

259
00:08:28,320 --> 00:08:29,521
但我觉得我可能下不了决心
but I think it might be hard for me

260
00:08:29,521 --> 00:08:31,888
让劫匪[钢人队]进监狱
to lock up a..."Steeler."

261
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:34,260
希望我没用力过猛
I try to keep it light.

262
00:08:34,645 --> 00:08:36,020
你介意我坐下吗
You might if I join you?

263
00:08:36,020 --> 00:08:37,900
不不不 这是自由的国家 坐
No, no, no, free country. Sit down.

264
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:39,160
他同意了
He said "Yes"!

265
00:08:39,980 --> 00:08:41,220
七十年代的橄榄球赛要精彩多了
The '70s, it was a better game.

266
00:08:41,280 --> 00:08:43,440
你们无所不能 进攻 防守
You guys did everything -- offense, defense.

267
00:08:43,720 --> 00:08:46,240
你有次是不是还在赛前给场地除草来着
Didn't I see you mow the field one night before the game?

268
00:08:46,380 --> 00:08:47,760
你知道我的钱就是靠除草赚来的吗
You know, that's how I made my money?

269
00:08:48,160 --> 00:08:49,920
我真不敢相信
I can't actually believe

270
00:08:49,920 --> 00:08:51,620
我在和特里·布拉德肖一起吃午餐
that I'm having lunch with Terry Bradshaw.

271
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:53,720
从橄榄球球星
I mean, from football fame

272
00:08:53,720 --> 00:08:56,740
到乡村音乐明星到著名演员
to country music stardom to big-screen idol.

273
00:08:56,858 --> 00:08:58,321
《横冲直撞斗飞车》续集
"Smokey and the Bandit II."

274
00:08:58,340 --> 00:09:00,999
演自己 真的是项挑战
Now that was a challenge. To play yourself,

275
00:09:00,999 --> 00:09:02,200
特别不好演
that can be kind of tricky.

276
00:09:02,200 --> 00:09:03,664
我认为整部戏焦点都到你身上了
I thought you stole the movies?

277
00:09:03,799 --> 00:09:05,240
别夸我了 你人太好了
Ah, stop that. You're too kind.

278
00:09:05,240 --> 00:09:07,480
我也不是做什么成什么的
You know, not everything I touch turns to gold.

279
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:10,064
我这辈子也有过不少失误
I mean, I've had my share of missteps along the way.

280
00:09:10,064 --> 00:09:11,720
是啊 例如《赖家王老五》 对吧
Well, right, like "Failure to Launch," right?

281
00:09:11,720 --> 00:09:13,280
-什么 -你是该不好意思
- Sorry? - You should be.

282
00:09:13,600 --> 00:09:15,240
那电影太差劲了
I mean, that thing was a real stinker.

283
00:09:15,420 --> 00:09:16,840
我偏偏很为那部电影自豪
I happen to be proud of that movie.

284
00:09:17,440 --> 00:09:19,160
那是我演得最好的电影之一
I mean, that's some of the best work I've ever done.

285
00:09:19,220 --> 00:09:20,740
你演得当然很好 没错
No, you were good, yeah.

286
00:09:20,740 --> 00:09:22,700
但演得好不好都没关系 反正没人看
But, I mean, don't worry about it. Nobody saw it.

287
00:09:22,920 --> 00:09:24,080
那好
Yeah, well.

288
00:09:24,600 --> 00:09:27,100
我想我们该回庭上了
Guess it's about time we get on back in, huh?

289
00:09:27,320 --> 00:09:28,140
明天这时候再见
Same time tomorrow.

290
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:30,000
我日程表上全是空挡
Hey, I'm wide open.

291
00:09:31,420 --> 00:09:32,300
像玩橄榄球时有空挡一样
Like in football.

292
00:09:36,840 --> 00:09:38,800
没人能对我儿子那么说话
Nobody speaks to my son like that.

293
00:09:39,320 --> 00:09:40,380
不 妈 妈 妈
No, no, Mom, Mom, Mom.

294
00:09:40,380 --> 00:09:43,060
求你别过去大闹一场让我更丢人
Please don't get up and make a scene and embarrass me more.

295
00:09:43,300 --> 00:09:43,800
我求你了
I'm begging you.

296
00:09:43,920 --> 00:09:45,540
好 但你没必要堵住我吧
Okay, but you don't have to block me in.

297
00:09:45,680 --> 00:09:46,620
我又不是疯婆子
I am not crazy.

298
00:09:46,720 --> 00:09:48,560
你们都以为我是个冲动的拉丁女人
I am not the hot-headed Latina

299
00:09:48,560 --> 00:09:49,980
但我不是那样的
that you all make me out to be.

300
00:09:50,080 --> 00:09:52,660
你给儿童足球裁判寄过一颗牛心
You sent a cow heart to a children's soccer referee.

301
00:09:52,980 --> 00:09:55,160
曼尼 不然我还能怎么警告他
Manny, what else was I supposed to do?

302
00:09:55,180 --> 00:09:56,880
刚刚那一幕也是好事
Look, what happened was a good thing.

303
00:09:56,960 --> 00:09:58,820
他在教我想做个艺术家
He was teaching me the focus required

304
00:09:58,820 --> 00:10:00,160
就要有这种专注力
to live the life of an artist,

305
00:10:00,360 --> 00:10:03,660
那是宝贵的一课 我会珍惜一辈子的
and that is a very valuable lesson that I'll cherish forever.

306
00:10:04,720 --> 00:10:06,420
好吧宝贝 如果你开心我就开心
Okay, Papi, if you're happy, then I'm happy.

307
00:10:08,580 --> 00:10:10,300
不如你挑份甜点吧
Why don't you pick your dessert?

308
00:10:12,900 --> 00:10:14,620
我不介意来块杏仁饼干
I wouldn't say no to an almond cookie

309
00:10:14,620 --> 00:10:15,639
一杯浓缩咖啡
and an espresso and...

310
00:10:15,639 --> 00:10:16,993
你已经不在了 是不是
And you're gone, aren't you?

311
00:10:18,678 --> 00:10:20,020
-亲爱的 再给我来份 -闭嘴
- Honey, I'll take another -- - Shut up.

312
00:10:20,020 --> 00:10:21,200
那是我儿子
That's my son over there.

313
00:10:21,420 --> 00:10:23,820
他对你赤诚相待
He opened his beautiful soul to you,

314
00:10:23,820 --> 00:10:26,520
赞美你 向你寻求建议
to praise you, to get some advice from you,

315
00:10:26,600 --> 00:10:27,720
你却对他这么刻薄
and you were mean to him?

316
00:10:28,160 --> 00:10:29,840
拜托 我们都知道你这态度
Come on, we both know that your attitude

317
00:10:29,840 --> 00:10:31,900
只是一种防卫机制
is just a defense mechanism

318
00:10:31,900 --> 00:10:34,660
保护你那小得可怜的自我
to protect the tiny, little ego

319
00:10:34,660 --> 00:10:36,340
不愿承认事实
from the truth --

320
00:10:36,780 --> 00:10:38,800
事实就是你根本不配任何赞美
that you don't deserve any praise,

321
00:10:39,220 --> 00:10:40,280
你是个骗子
that you're a fraud,

322
00:10:40,940 --> 00:10:43,440
一个无足轻重的大胖子而已
that you're just a big, fat nobody.

323
00:10:51,740 --> 00:10:53,660
所有男人都有一样的软肋
All men break the same.

324
00:11:06,240 --> 00:11:07,580
这是什么鬼 这是什么意思
What's happening? What is all this?

325
00:11:07,600 --> 00:11:08,940
-去下一个货架通道 -行
- Go up the next aisle. - Okay.

326
00:11:12,915 --> 00:11:13,960
天啊
Oh, God,

327
00:11:13,960 --> 00:11:15,440
我爱死我们新挑的地砖颜色了
I'm loving these new pavers we picked.

328
00:11:15,520 --> 00:11:17,423
其实我又有点犹豫了
You know what, I'm starting to have second thoughts.

329
00:11:17,423 --> 00:11:18,940
拜托
Oh, no, this isn't gonna be

330
00:11:18,940 --> 00:11:20,420
我们不是又要开始吵了吧
another conflict between us, is it?

331
00:11:20,420 --> 00:11:22,540
我的天 我可不想再和你吵了
Oh, gosh, I don't want another conflict.

332
00:11:23,734 --> 00:11:27,740
你不会真的想买
Okay, you're -- you're not actually putting

333
00:11:27,740 --> 00:11:30,054
这块再生木件吧
a reclaimed wood piece in our cart, are you?

334
00:11:30,054 --> 00:11:30,220
说得好 说得好
That's great, that's great.

335
00:11:30,220 --> 00:11:32,540
不 "再生木材美学"
No, the whole "reclaimed wood aesthetic"

336
00:11:32,540 --> 00:11:35,220
是对谷仓文化的侮辱性剽窃
is an insulting appropriation of barn culture.

337
00:11:35,460 --> 00:11:36,380
我是认真的
No, I'm being serious.

338
00:11:36,480 --> 00:11:38,100
就像麦当娜穿工装裤的效果
It's like when Madonna wore overalls!

339
00:11:38,480 --> 00:11:40,360
-太棒 -米奇尔 快拿走我不想要
- You're good. - Mitchell, take it out. I don't want it.

340
00:11:40,440 --> 00:11:41,220
我觉得挺好看的
I think it's pretty.

341
00:11:41,320 --> 00:11:42,535
我觉得这挺冒犯人的
I think it's pretty offensive.

342
00:11:42,535 --> 00:11:44,200
控制一下你的情绪
Okay, rein it in.

343
00:11:44,200 --> 00:11:45,758
看啊 修道院院长
Oh, there she is, Mother Superior.

344
00:11:45,758 --> 00:11:47,660
够了 脸皮薄星人
Okay, Rumple-thinskin.

345
00:11:47,660 --> 00:11:48,740
我不管了 我才不要吵
Okay, you know what? I don't need this.

346
00:11:48,740 --> 00:11:50,120
我现在就去车里等着
I'm just gonna go wait in the car.

347
00:11:50,120 --> 00:11:51,020
很好 逃走吧
Perfect, yeah, run away.

348
00:11:51,060 --> 00:11:53,520
只是告诉你一下 我喜欢谷仓木
And just FYI, the reason I like barn wood

349
00:11:53,520 --> 00:11:55,190
是因为它让我想到你
is 'cause it reminds me of you.

350
00:11:55,320 --> 00:11:56,258
-真的吗 -真的
- Really? - Yeah.

351
00:11:56,258 --> 00:11:58,514
我知道你有时候会很想家
I mean I-I know that you get homesick sometimes,

352
00:11:58,514 --> 00:11:59,201
我就想给家里增添一点
and I-I want to bring

353
00:11:59,201 --> 00:12:00,800
一点乡村的气息
a little, you know, country into our house.

354
00:12:00,800 --> 00:12:01,440
对不起
I'm sorry.

355
00:12:01,700 --> 00:12:02,420
我不是有意要惹你生气的
Didn't mean to offend you.

356
00:12:02,860 --> 00:12:04,180
我没生气
Oh, you didn't offend me.

357
00:12:04,240 --> 00:12:06,260
我只是像你说的太玻璃心了
I'm just being oversensitive like you said.

358
00:12:06,391 --> 00:12:08,344
我也是又开始骄傲自大了
I'm just being my normal snooty self.

359
00:12:08,344 --> 00:12:10,460
真不知道你是怎么一直忍让我的
I don't -- I don't know how you put up with me.

360
00:12:10,460 --> 00:12:11,620
是我不知道你怎么能一直忍我
I don't know how you put up with me.

361
00:12:11,820 --> 00:12:12,300
我知道
I do.

362
00:12:14,220 --> 00:12:14,996
不好意思
Excuse me.

363
00:12:14,996 --> 00:12:17,480
-什么事 -怎么了 你好啊
- Oh. Yes? - Oh, yes? Hi.

364
00:12:17,480 --> 00:12:18,558
我就是想借过一下
I just need to get by.

365
00:12:18,558 --> 00:12:19,707
-行 -没问题
- Okay. - Okay.

366
00:12:22,380 --> 00:12:23,880
他没有说那句话
He didn't say it.

367
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:25,060
他没说
He didn't say it.

368
00:12:25,480 --> 00:12:29,380
最后就是 这里尽览全城美景
And last, but not least, the city at your feet.

369
00:12:30,260 --> 00:12:32,320
我还是挺吃惊的
Yeah. I'm still kind of flabbergasted

370
00:12:32,320 --> 00:12:33,640
这里竟然没有泡沫机
that there's no bubble machine.

371
00:12:34,080 --> 00:12:35,560
没关系 我可以自己装一个
It's okay. I can install my own.

372
00:12:36,639 --> 00:12:38,401
-你在鄙视我吗 -没有
- Oh, you're judging me? - No, no.

373
00:12:39,760 --> 00:12:40,840
可能你是对的
Maybe you're right.

374
00:12:41,480 --> 00:12:43,360
我可能的确越来越不食人间烟火了
Maybe I am losing touch with who I am.

375
00:12:43,580 --> 00:12:45,560
人生只需要一把三弦吉他和一张床垫
All I really need is three chords and a mattress.

376
00:12:45,560 --> 00:12:46,760
还有我的主厨就行了
And my chef.

377
00:12:49,660 --> 00:12:51,340
菲尔 你怎么了
Uh, hey, Phil, what's happening here?

378
00:12:51,420 --> 00:12:53,300
-拜托别加重 -菲尔
- Oh, not too much. - Phil?

379
00:12:53,820 --> 00:12:55,080
我的天 你脸都憋黄了
Oh, my God, you've gone all yellow.

380
00:12:55,742 --> 00:12:56,840
和你的歌名一样
That's like your song.

381
00:12:56,840 --> 00:13:00,021
真巧... 我也想写歌...
Funny thing -- I also like to write mu--

382
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:02,440
菲尔
Phil?

383
00:13:09,800 --> 00:13:10,680
我怎么了
What happened?

384
00:13:10,880 --> 00:13:13,000
邓菲先生 你得了急性睾丸炎
Mr. Dunphy, you have acute orchitis.

385
00:13:13,240 --> 00:13:14,679
睾丸大面积发炎
It's a massively inflamed testicle.

386
00:13:14,679 --> 00:13:16,380
我在给你打抗生素点滴
I'm giving you an I.V. bag of antibiotics

387
00:13:16,380 --> 00:13:17,700
也给你开了止痛药 因为...
and some pain meds because...

388
00:13:19,020 --> 00:13:19,340
太惨了
Oh, boy.

389
00:13:19,920 --> 00:13:20,500
真丢人
So embarrassed.

390
00:13:20,700 --> 00:13:22,814
不敢相信我晕倒在摇滚巨星面前
I can't believe I passed out in front of a rock star.

391
00:13:22,814 --> 00:13:25,140
请告诉我他不知道我晕倒的原因
Please tell me he didn't know why.

392
00:13:25,140 --> 00:13:26,172
太棒了 你醒了
Oh, brilliant, you're awake.

393
00:13:26,172 --> 00:13:28,160
我给你的蛋蛋拿了点冰来
I've got some ice for your biscuits.

394
00:13:28,160 --> 00:13:29,960
不要啊 不 别别别
No. No, no, no, no, no!

395
00:13:29,960 --> 00:13:31,700
太丢人了 咦 还真的...
Oh! Oh, that really --

396
00:13:31,780 --> 00:13:33,020
还真的挺舒服的
Oh, that feels so good.

397
00:13:34,900 --> 00:13:37,520
特里 能聊聊吗 拜托别不理我
Terry, can we talk? Please don't shut me out.

398
00:13:37,780 --> 00:13:38,900
我知道我做错了
I know I messed up,

399
00:13:38,900 --> 00:13:41,280
我对我午餐时的表现
and I'm so sorry for my...

400
00:13:41,280 --> 00:13:42,280
非常抱歉[赖家王老五]
failure at lunch.

401
00:13:43,040 --> 00:13:45,200
-先生 请坐下 -能让一个位置吗
- Sir, please sit down. - Do you mind?

402
00:13:45,800 --> 00:13:46,620
不得换座
Same seats.

403
00:13:47,140 --> 00:13:48,000
继续开庭
Let's proceed.

404
00:13:48,417 --> 00:13:50,000
陪审员10号
Juror number 10,

405
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:51,420
你的家里
has anyone in your family

406
00:13:51,420 --> 00:13:53,380
有没有人曾经是暴力犯罪的受害者
ever been the victim of a violent crime?

407
00:13:53,800 --> 00:13:56,380
我的母亲...
Well...my mother...

408
00:13:56,560 --> 00:13:58,138
-嘿 - 没叫你 你继续说
- Psst! - Not you, keep going.

409
00:13:58,138 --> 00:13:58,880
对了
Oh, actually,

410
00:13:58,880 --> 00:14:00,078
你能不能拍他肩膀叫他一下
could you tap him on the shoulder?

411
00:14:00,078 --> 00:14:02,569
陪审员11号 这个男人是在骚扰你吗
Juror 11, is this man bothering you?

412
00:14:02,569 --> 00:14:04,412
你是说这个影评人吗
You talking about the movie critic right here?

413
00:14:04,412 --> 00:14:06,380
-当然了 他就是在骚扰我 -反对
- Absolutely, he's bothering me! - Objection!

414
00:14:06,380 --> 00:14:08,280
我请求接近布拉德肖先生的许可
I request permission to approach Mr. Bradshaw.

415
00:14:08,320 --> 00:14:09,909
不行 请求驳回
No! I mean, denied!

416
00:14:09,909 --> 00:14:11,842
这不是你能请求的事情
Look, that's not a thing you can ask.

417
00:14:11,853 --> 00:14:14,520
法官大人 我们想请陪审员3号离席
Your Honor, we'd like to dismiss Juror number 3.

418
00:14:14,520 --> 00:14:15,580
什么 不不
What?! No, no.

419
00:14:15,580 --> 00:14:16,440
我不会再这样了 我保证
I'll be good. I promise.

420
00:14:16,660 --> 00:14:18,500
先生 现在请您离开
Sir, you have to leave now.

421
00:14:19,420 --> 00:14:19,820
好吧
Fine.

422
00:14:20,420 --> 00:14:21,140
我走
I'm going.

423
00:14:24,320 --> 00:14:26,320
老兄 我会在停车场等着你的
I'll be waiting in the parking lot, buddy.

424
00:14:27,500 --> 00:14:29,200
法官给我发了限制令
Judge hit me with a restraining order.

425
00:14:29,880 --> 00:14:31,440
但泰瑞得签名
But Terry had to sign it.

426
00:14:34,217 --> 00:14:35,820
我们会一起度过此劫的 菲利普
We're gonna get through this together, Phillip.

427
00:14:35,820 --> 00:14:38,560
我不懂你为什么要在这里
I guess I just don't understand why you're here.

428
00:14:38,780 --> 00:14:40,439
因为是你让我警醒
Well, because you really reached me back there,

429
00:14:40,439 --> 00:14:42,600
我得做回个正常人
and I realized I got to be more of a regular guy.

430
00:14:42,600 --> 00:14:44,800
邓菲 我有... 克里斯·马汀
Mr. Dunphy, I have your -- Chris Martin.

431
00:14:45,460 --> 00:14:46,840
我是你的粉丝
Wow. I'm a huge fan.

432
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:48,500
-我能和你合个影吗 -不行
- Can I get a picture with you? - No.

433
00:14:48,680 --> 00:14:49,960
是我想和你合影
I want a picture with you.

434
00:14:49,980 --> 00:14:50,940
来吧
Come on.

435
00:14:51,160 --> 00:14:52,120
开始
Let's do it.

436
00:14:52,120 --> 00:14:54,280
菲尔 我有两千五百万粉丝
Phil, 25 million followers.

437
00:14:54,540 --> 00:14:55,242
别了 谢谢你
No, thank you.

438
00:14:55,242 --> 00:14:56,860
-我需要私人空间 -好啦
- Uh, I'd love some privacy. - All right.

439
00:14:56,860 --> 00:14:59,160
还有空闲房间吗
Is there maybe a room opening up?

440
00:14:59,460 --> 00:15:00,460
菲尔 亲爱的
Phil? Honey?

441
00:15:00,500 --> 00:15:02,500
克里斯一打电话 我就赶来了
I came just as soon as Chris called me.

442
00:15:02,500 --> 00:15:03,297
你好
Hello.

443
00:15:03,297 --> 00:15:04,673
克莱尔 我不得不说
Claire, I've got to say, uh...

444
00:15:05,080 --> 00:15:06,339
你比菲尔的照片里
You're even more beautiful

445
00:15:06,339 --> 00:15:07,869
更漂亮
than you are in Phil's photos.

446
00:15:09,350 --> 00:15:10,780
-我很喜欢你的音乐 -谢谢
- I like your music. - Well, thank you.

447
00:15:10,780 --> 00:15:11,880
克莱尔 我能和你说几句话不
Claire, can I talk to you for one second.

448
00:15:11,880 --> 00:15:13,320
当然啦 亲爱的
Yes, of course, sweetie, yes.

449
00:15:14,580 --> 00:15:16,577
我希望克里斯·马汀离开
I want Chris Martin to leave.

450
00:15:16,577 --> 00:15:18,160
什么 为什么
Hm? What? Why?

451
00:15:18,160 --> 00:15:19,960
我这样子的时候 他在这里好奇怪
It's weird that he's here when I'm like this,

452
00:15:19,960 --> 00:15:21,241
而且他把大家都吸引来了
and he's attracting attention.

453
00:15:21,241 --> 00:15:23,413
我觉得不... 好吧
Oh, I don't think... yeah, okay.

454
00:15:24,112 --> 00:15:25,227
克莱尔
Claire? Mm...

455
00:15:25,660 --> 00:15:27,780
你可能不会喜欢这个
Oh, you're not gonna like this.

456
00:15:28,548 --> 00:15:31,700
-太激动啦 -你邀请了你读书会的人吗
- This is so exciting! - You invited your book club?!

457
00:15:31,700 --> 00:15:33,180
我们超喜欢你
We're huge fans.

458
00:15:33,940 --> 00:15:36,240
读书会听起来很平民化
A book club sounds kind of regular.

459
00:15:36,540 --> 00:15:37,757
我也应该加入一个
I should join one of those.

460
00:15:37,757 --> 00:15:39,740
我们即将有空缺
There's about to be an opening in ours.

461
00:15:39,740 --> 00:15:41,080
是我邀请你们来的
I'm the one who invited you here.

462
00:15:41,342 --> 00:15:43,691
美丽的智慧女性们 你们都读什么呢
And what are you beautiful, uh, scholars reading?

463
00:15:43,691 --> 00:15:45,486
《不知情的卡斯尔小姐》
"The Unwitting Miss Castle."

464
00:15:46,195 --> 00:15:47,350
我喜欢这本书
Mm. I love that book.

465
00:15:47,660 --> 00:15:50,540
但我觉得里面栅栏的比喻
Although I did find the fences metaphor

466
00:15:50,540 --> 00:15:51,360
略俗
a little mundane.

467
00:15:51,562 --> 00:15:53,740
-是啊 太做作了 -完全同意
- Oh, yes. Pretentious. - Completely agree.

468
00:15:53,740 --> 00:15:55,580
上周我说了一模一样的话
I said the exact same thing last week,

469
00:15:55,580 --> 00:15:57,920
你们却冲我翻白眼
and you guys just rolled your eyes at me.

470
00:15:58,303 --> 00:16:00,005
克莱尔 别和德弗罗夫人似的
Claire, don't be such a Mrs. Devereaux.

471
00:16:00,372 --> 00:16:01,954
-太像啦 太夸张了 -菲尔
- Twinsies! That is so you! - Hey, Phil.

472
00:16:02,105 --> 00:16:03,823
我们照片有两万五千个赞啦
Our photo got 25,000 likes.

473
00:16:04,230 --> 00:16:04,966
菲尔
Phil?

474
00:16:05,460 --> 00:16:05,940
菲尔
Phil?

475
00:16:08,280 --> 00:16:10,740
可能是因为药物的作用
Oh, it's probably all the meds.

476
00:16:11,120 --> 00:16:11,940
放着我来
I'll handle this.

477
00:16:12,060 --> 00:16:13,517
我曾和基思·理查兹去过狂欢节
I've been to Burning Man with Keith Richards.

478
00:16:13,517 --> 00:16:15,023
不不 还是我来
No, no, no. I'll handle it.

479
00:16:15,080 --> 00:16:16,700
我可是和我疯子妈一起度过假
I've been on vacation with my mother.

480
00:16:18,980 --> 00:16:22,300
你要去哪呀 陌生人
Hey. Where are you off to, stranger?

481
00:16:22,440 --> 00:16:23,600
亲爱的 我得一个人待会
Honey, I need to be alone.

482
00:16:23,920 --> 00:16:25,660
亲爱的 对不起 我不该
Oh, honey, I'm sorry I invited

483
00:16:25,660 --> 00:16:26,581
邀请读书会的姑娘们
the girls from book club.

484
00:16:26,581 --> 00:16:28,683
我就是想让她们喜欢我
It's -- I just wanted them to like me.

485
00:16:28,820 --> 00:16:30,139
我不敢相信这真的发生了
I can't believe this happened.

486
00:16:30,139 --> 00:16:33,200
-这本应该是很棒的一天 -我知道
- This was supposed to be such an amazing day. - I know.

487
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:34,700
有没有什么我能做的
Is there anything I can do to make it better?

488
00:16:34,940 --> 00:16:37,920
你可以让克里斯·马汀离开 就现在
Yes. You can make Chris Martin go away, now.

489
00:16:40,020 --> 00:16:41,339
对不起 亲们
I'm so sorry, guys.

490
00:16:41,339 --> 00:16:43,107
-我不是故意要引起 -不不不
- Oh, I didn't mean to cause a -- - Oh, no, no, no, no.

491
00:16:43,107 --> 00:16:44,805
不是因为你这个人有问题
It's -- it's not you personally.

492
00:16:44,805 --> 00:16:46,980
不不 就是我的问题 我老让别人分心
No, no, no, it is me. I'm a distraction.

493
00:16:46,980 --> 00:16:47,920
每个人都想打招呼
Everyone wants to say "Hi"

494
00:16:47,920 --> 00:16:48,860
或者合照
or they want to take a picture

495
00:16:48,860 --> 00:16:49,800
或者睡我
or they want to sleep with me.

496
00:16:50,020 --> 00:16:50,979
她们真的想
They sure do.

497
00:16:50,979 --> 00:16:52,255
得了 玛丽
Shut 'er down, Marie.

498
00:16:52,680 --> 00:16:53,660
简直是场噩梦
And it's a nightmare.

499
00:16:53,900 --> 00:16:55,420
这开始影响到我的创造力
It's beginning to affect my creativity.

500
00:16:55,920 --> 00:16:57,740
我写的最新一首歌是关于我的直升机
The last song I wrote was about my helicopter.

501
00:16:58,400 --> 00:16:59,801
我实在没脸发行
I was too ashamed to release it.

502
00:16:59,801 --> 00:17:01,892
我不得不卖给澳洲航空 卖了一百万
I had to sell it to Qantus for $1 million.

503
00:17:01,892 --> 00:17:04,080
你的问题好枯苗望雨
Your problems are so sanguine.

504
00:17:04,080 --> 00:17:05,300
这个词是这么用的吗
Is that how you use that word?

505
00:17:05,700 --> 00:17:06,480
没人知道
Nobody knows.

506
00:17:07,460 --> 00:17:08,820
总之 我希望我能做些什么
Oh, anyway, I wish there was something I could do

507
00:17:08,820 --> 00:17:09,640
让这有所改善
to make this all better.

508
00:17:09,860 --> 00:17:10,880
你可以买下那间房子
You could buy that house.

509
00:17:11,020 --> 00:17:11,900
不 菲尔
No, Phil.

510
00:17:11,900 --> 00:17:13,200
谢谢你 那是我过去的做法
Thanks to you, that's the old me.

511
00:17:13,560 --> 00:17:14,480
好吧
Oh, good.

512
00:17:14,860 --> 00:17:16,480
我知道你可以为他做什么
I know something you could do for him.

513
00:17:18,283 --> 00:17:20,999
♪ 你一直寻找属于你的独特空间 ♪
♪ You've been looking for your own special space ♪

514
00:17:21,420 --> 00:17:24,625
♪ 可称为栖息之所的地方 ♪
♪ Somewhere you can call your resting place ♪

515
00:17:25,301 --> 00:17:28,271
♪ 你一直为了孩子和爱人寻找 ♪
♪ You've been looking for your kids and your spouse ♪

516
00:17:29,104 --> 00:17:31,898
♪ 是时候给自己买套邓菲推荐的房子 ♪
♪ It's time time to buy yourself a Dunphy house ♪

517
00:17:33,770 --> 00:17:37,838
♪ 邓菲 邓菲 邓菲 ♪
♪ Oh, Dunphy, Dunphy, Dunphy ♪

518
00:17:40,739 --> 00:17:46,335
♪ 价格实惠又舒适 舒适 舒适 ♪
♪ They're affordable and comfy, comfy, comfy ♪

519
00:17:47,100 --> 00:17:48,473
真不敢相信他能让这种歌好听
I can't believe he's actually making it work.

520
00:17:48,473 --> 00:17:51,602
♪ 邓菲 邓菲 邓菲 ♪
♪ Oh, Dunphy, Dunphy, Dunphy ♪

521
00:17:51,700 --> 00:17:52,680
那他为什么会不选我们
Why would he not pick us?

522
00:17:52,740 --> 00:17:54,000
对啊 他想要的我们都有
Yeah, we gave him everything he wants --

523
00:17:54,080 --> 00:17:55,200
能吵架 能和好
a fight, reconciliation...

524
00:17:55,360 --> 00:17:56,640
而且我们上镜毫无压力
...not to mention we're camera-ready.

525
00:17:56,760 --> 00:17:58,240
电视节目想要的全都符合
It's everything TV wants to be.

526
00:17:58,320 --> 00:17:59,440
他还要我们怎么样啊
I mean, what does he want us to do,

527
00:17:59,540 --> 00:18:00,460
帮他写好整集的脚本吗
write the episode for him?

528
00:18:00,460 --> 00:18:03,020
美国民众应该有看我们得到小凉亭的机会
Yeah, America deserves to see us get a free gazebo.

529
00:18:03,180 --> 00:18:03,720
他在那里
There he is.

530
00:18:04,040 --> 00:18:05,860
我心里有5成想去跟他撕逼
I have half a mind to go over there and confront him.

531
00:18:05,920 --> 00:18:07,151
我心里有另外5成
Yeah, well, I have the other half.

532
00:18:07,151 --> 00:18:09,440
-等等 -你好
- Wait, wait. - Hi.

533
00:18:09,440 --> 00:18:10,700
-不好意思 -有何能效劳吗
- Excuse us. - Can I help you guys?

534
00:18:10,800 --> 00:18:11,880
给我们个解释如何
Yeah, how about an explanation.

535
00:18:12,500 --> 00:18:14,020
你为什么不选我们上你节目
Why aren't you picking us for your show?

536
00:18:14,220 --> 00:18:15,320
我们不够性感帅气吗
Yeah, what -- are we not sexy enough?

537
00:18:15,360 --> 00:18:16,903
还是不够小鲜肉
Not young enough for your demo?

538
00:18:16,903 --> 00:18:18,140
等等 难道是因为我们是同性恋吗
Wait, no, is it 'cause we're gay?

539
00:18:18,140 --> 00:18:19,540
我好像没有看过同性恋情侣
You know, I've actually never seen a gay couple

540
00:18:19,540 --> 00:18:20,440
上你的节目
on your little program.

541
00:18:20,540 --> 00:18:22,560
也没看过体育老师兼副校长上过
Yeah, or a P.E. Teacher-slash-vice principal.

542
00:18:22,680 --> 00:18:24,320
-他就是 -你就直说为何不选我们
- He's literally that. - Just tell us why you're not picking us.

543
00:18:24,340 --> 00:18:25,740
两位 我已经没有节目了
Guys, I don't have a show anymore.

544
00:18:25,980 --> 00:18:27,681
-少来 我们刚看完你... -对啊
- Please, we just saw that episode -- Yeah.

545
00:18:27,681 --> 00:18:30,001
-上周圣安东尼奥市的小黛与小唐那集 -对啊
- Deb and Don in San Antonio last week? - Yeah.

546
00:18:30,001 --> 00:18:31,500
小唐想要能烧烤的地方
Oh... Don wanted a place to grill.

547
00:18:31,500 --> 00:18:33,615
-我们节目两年前就停了 -什么
- We got canceled, like, two years ago. - What?

548
00:18:33,615 --> 00:18:35,740
-什么 -这节目不是很火吗
- What, why? - Yeah. It's such a popular show!

549
00:18:35,740 --> 00:18:37,120
是这样的...
Look, uh...

550
00:18:37,620 --> 00:18:39,136
电视台把我炒了
The network fired me...

551
00:18:39,136 --> 00:18:40,280
-为什么 -他们发现我
- Why? - when they found out

552
00:18:40,280 --> 00:18:42,160
建了一个网站让观众付费
that I had this website where people paid

553
00:18:42,160 --> 00:18:43,640
看我裸体造东西
to watch me build stuff naked.

554
00:18:43,740 --> 00:18:44,920
-是吗 -是啊
- Is that so? - Yeah.

555
00:18:44,920 --> 00:18:45,440
裸到哪种程度
How naked?

556
00:18:46,120 --> 00:18:46,512
非常
Very.

557
00:18:46,512 --> 00:18:47,700
那你为什么还在
You know what, why are you hanging out

558
00:18:47,700 --> 00:18:48,800
家居卖场里晃悠呢
in the aisles of a home store?

559
00:18:49,100 --> 00:18:49,940
我在这里工作
I work here.

560
00:18:50,380 --> 00:18:51,320
-还真是 -是啊
- You do. - Yeah.

561
00:18:51,354 --> 00:18:55,015
-那如果你节目还在... -然后呢
- Hey, if you did still have a show, um... - Uh-huh?

562
00:18:55,140 --> 00:18:55,880
你会请我们上吗
...would you pick us?

563
00:18:57,900 --> 00:18:59,920
你说"愿意"不会死好吗
It costs you nothing to say "Yes."

564
00:19:00,160 --> 00:19:01,560
天啊 我们又心灵相通了
Oh, my God, we agreed again.

565
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:06,960
我求过你别去了
I begged you not to go over there.

566
00:19:06,960 --> 00:19:08,140
我现在好羞愧
I'm so embarrassed.

567
00:19:08,260 --> 00:19:08,740
羞愧什么
Why?

568
00:19:09,460 --> 00:19:10,560
他才是在哇哇哭的人
He's the one crying.

569
00:19:10,940 --> 00:19:11,821
我最爱的部分就是
My favorite part was

570
00:19:11,821 --> 00:19:14,580
看他边哭边想喘气时
when he was gasping for air between sobs,

571
00:19:14,580 --> 00:19:15,540
那像小婴儿的样子
like a baby.

572
00:19:15,560 --> 00:19:17,000
你看他 心都碎了
Look at him. He's broken.

573
00:19:17,880 --> 00:19:19,500
万一他从此封笔了怎么办
What if he never writes again?

574
00:19:19,580 --> 00:19:21,850
行 那我就去跟全世界剩下的
Okay, I'll apologize to the 12 people

575
00:19:21,850 --> 00:19:23,780
12个还在看戏剧演出的人道歉
who still go out and watch plays.

576
00:19:23,780 --> 00:19:25,059
你知道我也是戏剧专业的吧
You do know I'm a theater major, right?

577
00:19:25,059 --> 00:19:27,400
是啊 所以当你哪天变成大编剧
Yes, and when you're a great play writer

578
00:19:27,400 --> 00:19:28,700
然后也去到一家餐厅时
and you go to a restaurant --

579
00:19:29,120 --> 00:19:30,240
前提是你下得起馆子
if you can afford it --

580
00:19:30,400 --> 00:19:32,500
到时候你就得礼貌对待陌生粉丝
then you're gonna be nice to strangers,

581
00:19:32,500 --> 00:19:34,700
因为这才是正确的待粉之道 懂了吗
because that's the right thing to do, okay?

582
00:19:35,480 --> 00:19:36,840
抱歉 我不是有意要打扰
Excuse me. I don't mean to interrupt.

583
00:19:36,940 --> 00:19:40,340
但我看到刚才发生的事了 我为你感到遗憾
But I saw what happened before, and I'm sorry about that.

584
00:19:40,340 --> 00:19:42,360
但你挺身而出 去训了那贱人一顿
But the way you stood up to that jerk Anvilmaker

585
00:19:42,400 --> 00:19:44,240
真的是大快人心
was kind of amazing, yeah.

586
00:19:44,240 --> 00:19:45,040
为你点赞
Good for you.

587
00:19:45,240 --> 00:19:46,280
小兄弟听我说
And young man, listen --

588
00:19:46,340 --> 00:19:47,708
希望这能安慰到你
if this makes you feel any better,

589
00:19:47,708 --> 00:19:49,644
其实他也那么对待我过
he did the same thing to me. Oh.

590
00:19:50,120 --> 00:19:51,680
谢谢您的一番美言
That's very nice of you to say.

591
00:19:51,680 --> 00:19:54,620
十分感谢您的鼓励
Thank you so much. So...

592
00:19:54,620 --> 00:19:58,340
其实呢... 我也写作
You know, I, uh... I write.

593
00:19:58,600 --> 00:19:59,240
要命
Oh, boy.

594
00:19:59,880 --> 00:20:01,860
我不是那种... 那种...
No, it's not like I'm just some, you know, some --

595
00:20:01,900 --> 00:20:02,940
过去一下 那种...
excuse me -- some --

596
00:20:02,940 --> 00:20:05,080
那种乱吹牛逼的老滑头
you know, just some city slicker who --

597
00:20:05,080 --> 00:20:06,790
毛都不懂就胡吹乱盖
who doesn't know what he's talking about.

598
00:20:06,790 --> 00:20:09,073
但如果我能传授你一招
But, uh... if I could teach you one thing,

599
00:20:09,073 --> 00:20:12,340
就这一招 如果你能学会
just one thing that you learn from this,

600
00:20:12,340 --> 00:20:16,740
你的剧就能够变得活灵活现
it'll make your plays sound and look marvelous.

601
00:20:16,760 --> 00:20:17,580
知道了吗
You know?

602
00:20:20,900 --> 00:20:23,765
所以最重要的一件事就是...
So, the most important thing is to --

603
00:20:23,765 --> 00:20:26,080
认识到创作其实就是改写
is to know that writing is really re-writing.

604
00:20:26,080 --> 00:20:27,760
这句箴言你最好写下来
You may want to jot that down.

605
00:20:28,007 --> 00:20:29,094
然后再"修改"
Uh... And then change it.

606
00:20:29,988 --> 00:20:30,960
听出我这句话的哏了吗
Did you see what I did there?

607
00:20:30,960 --> 00:20:34,302
抱歉 我们真的有事得先走了
You know what? We really need to be somewhere right now.

608
00:20:34,302 --> 00:20:35,587
-对啊 别迟到了 -好的
- Yeah, we better go. - Okay.

609
00:20:35,587 --> 00:20:36,513
-是啊 -没事
- Yeah. - All right.

610
00:20:37,899 --> 00:20:38,778
谢谢你
Okay, thank you.

611
00:20:40,340 --> 00:20:43,141
真的对不起 我之前没意识到我们多烦人
I'm sorry, we didn't realize we were so annoying.

612
00:20:43,141 --> 00:20:44,178
是我们不对
Our bad.

613
00:20:46,220 --> 00:20:47,700
祝下笔如神 势如破竹
Have fun storming the castle!

614
00:20:48,840 --> 00:20:49,480
没回应
Nothing.

615
00:20:50,120 --> 00:20:51,040
老子要去落发修面了
I'm gonna shave.

616
00:20:52,886 --> 00:20:55,340
♪ 来感受那刺激 激 激 ♪
♪ Come feel the thrill, thrill, thrill ♪

617
00:20:57,604 --> 00:20:59,484
♪ 的菲尔 尔 尔 ♪
♪ Of Phil, Phil, Phil ♪

618
00:21:01,680 --> 00:21:04,800
♪ 那刺激 激 激 ♪
♪ The thrill, thrill, thrill ♪

619
00:21:06,049 --> 00:21:07,433
♪ 菲尔的刺激 ♪
♪ The thrill of Phil ♪

620
00:21:10,800 --> 00:21:12,520
能麻烦去把那声音关掉吗
Could you turn that down please?

621
00:21:14,580 --> 00:21:15,180
大家一起来
Everybody.

622
00:21:23,940 --> 00:21:26,020
我有几个小想法
So, a couple quick thoughts.
